+# Research Engine — Phase 6: The research agent (09-10-2026)
+
+**Source:** the Research Engine audit (`RESEARCH-ENGINE-AUDIT-2026-10-08.md`, section K, Phase 6; the execution router ⑩ of section F), on top of Phases 1–5. The outcome it set: *the Research Engine as an operating system the researcher directs in plain language and approves step by step.* Every change has a regression test and the tests were mutation-checked. Nothing existing was removed: the copilot's change plan, the Changes review, History and its rollback, the output route and the Findings tab are as they were; the agent sits on top of them and uses them — a workflow step is a proposal like any other, a document is the Phase 5 output, a model step is a model turn.
+
+## Checklist
+
+| ID | Audit finding (§D.5, §F ③/⑩, §K) | Change | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| A1 | No planner runs the end-to-end workflow from one objective; each request is read on its own | `packages/engine/src/researchPlanner.ts`: `researchWorkflow(def, { objective?, runAvailable?, produced?, mode? })` reads the survey as it is into twelve ordered steps — objective → assumptions → structured hypotheses → research framework → questionnaire → variables → analysis plan → crosstab and test recommendations → reporting framework → design document → survey structure → deck — each **done**, **ready** (the engine's own actions, for approval), **needs_input** (only the researcher can say, with an example sentence that records it), **model** (a language model would do it) or **blocked** (an earlier step first, named). Pure: it writes nothing and calls nothing | ✅ Added |
+| A2 | Steps that need prose are the model's; the rest must not wait for one | the engine does by itself: record the objective; read the population from the objective's words and the methodology from its goal (as assumptions, listed); record the readings parsed from a hypothesis; name a construct per hypothesis side (as a noun — *satisfied* → Satisfaction) with the questions that already measure it (by word family, or the standard measure's own words — "better value for money" measures Price perception); add a standard item for an unmeasured construct the library knows (and link the construct to it in the same approval); plan a mean score for a multi-item construct; propose the plan; add the test a measured hypothesis lacks (a construct's score, else the regression over its items, before a single item's correlation) and a missing priority-1 crosstab; read the KPIs from the dependent constructs (the measure from the level, the direction from the name); produce the proposal and the deck; move a screening question to the first block and a mid-survey demographic to the last. The model is asked only to draft hypotheses when none exist, to structure one the words cannot be read into, and to write a question for a construct with no standard item | ✅ Added |
+| A3 | No user-controllable Internal ↔ Cloud switch | the project setting `surveys.settings.ai.mode` (`internal` \| `cloud`), read and written by `POST /api/copilot/workflow` (`setMode`, `survey.edit`; the sandbox keeps it in the browser), switched in the Workflow tab. **Internal:** nothing is sent to a language model — a model turn is refused on its card with the cause and where the switch is (`internal_mode`, a failure code of its own, not "no model configured"), a sentence with an engine alternative gets the alternative (the standard items, the objective), a workflow model step becomes a question to the researcher, the findings outputs skip the narrative. **Per request:** one request let through to the cloud (the tab's "once" box, used up by the call that takes it), and `mode` on the route for one reading | ✅ Added |
+| A4 | One model, no tiers | `AI_MODEL_SMALL` (the small tier, for a short structuring reply) beside `AI_MODEL` (the large tier, drafting); `aiModelName(tier)`, `completeJson(…, { tier })`; the meter's estimate and reservation carry the tier (`AiEstimate.tier` → `aiSpec`), so the preview and the wallet see the same model; a step says which tier it needs | ✅ Added |
+| A5 | No cost preview before a cloud step | every model step carries what it would be asked (the prompt's size, the reply's cap, the operation); the route prices each through `estimateAi` — nothing reserved — and the tab shows the model and the credits next to the button that runs it, and the total of the cloud steps from here; in internal mode the line says the steps are the researcher's instead | ✅ Added |
+| A6 | Audit trail and rollback for agent steps | each step goes through the existing machinery: an engine step is a proposal in Changes (apply, exclude, cancel), recorded in History with `workflow: <step>` in its intent; an output step is the Phase 5 output; a model step is a model turn with its call and charge; a step rolls back like any change and the workflow shows it to do again | ✅ Reused |
+| A7 | The workflow by sentence | the engine reads *start the research workflow for …*, *plan the whole study for …*, *run the workflow*, *what's next?*, *where are we in the research workflow* into a `workflow` interpretation: the card says where the study stands (every step with its status and reason, the execution mode, the priced model steps) and the Workflow tab opens; an edit in the same sentence stays the model's | ✅ Added |
+
+## What was built
+
+**The planner (`packages/engine/src/researchPlanner.ts`)** — `researchWorkflow` builds the steps in order, each from the survey and the steps before it: a step is blocked by the first unmet prerequisite (the hypotheses by the objective, the framework by the hypotheses, the questionnaire by the framework, the recommendations by the plan, the deck by the plan and by fieldwork data). `next` is the first step not done; `summary` says how many are done and what the next one needs ("the engine has 2 actions ready", "the model is asked (large call)", "you are asked", "waits on analysis plan"). `describeWorkflow` is the card's text; `modelSteps` lists what the cost preview prices. `populationFromObjective` reads "UK adults who bought a car" out of "Understand why UK adults who bought a car switch from Brand A to Brand B" (the noun, its modifiers, the relative clause up to the sentence's own verb); `constructName` names a side as a noun; `questionsMeasuring` finds the questions that already measure a name. In internal mode a model step keeps its sentence (so "once" can let it through) but asks the researcher.
+
+**Tiers (`packages/ai`)** — `aiModelName("small" | "large")`; `completeJson` sends the tier's model. **The meter (`apps/studio/lib/aiEstimate.ts`)** — the estimate spec, carved out of `metering.ts` so it can be tested without a server: the tier's model is what is priced and reserved; under cost simulation the fake provider's "fake" report is priced at the configured model, but a real model name — the tier's — is kept.
+
+**The route (`POST /api/copilot/workflow`)** — `project.read`; the sandbox against the fake provider sends its own definition. It gives the planner what only the server knows (fieldwork completes, the project's mode) and returns the workflow, the mode (project, effective, whether a request override applied), the model (configured, provider, small, large), the cost per model step and the total, and `runAvailable`. The planner runs in the Studio too, on the survey as it stands in the editor (the open proposal included), so a step applied is done at once; the route's facts are read when the tab opens, on refresh, when the mode changes, and when a model step appears that has not been priced.
+
+**The Studio** — `useCopilot`: `executionMode` / `setExecutionMode`, `cloudOnce` / `setCloudOnce`, `workflow` (the planner on `working`), `workflowInfo`, `refreshWorkflow`, `showWorkflow` (the `workflow` interpretation), `runWorkflowStep` (an engine step → `local` as a proposal with `workflow: <step>` in its intent; an output step → `makeOutput`, which marks the document or the deck produced; a model step → `ask`); the internal-mode gate in `run` before any request leaves. `WorkflowTab` (`cp-tab-workflow`): the summary, the Internal / Cloud switch with the configured models, the cost line, the twelve steps with their marks, reasons, buttons (`wf-do-<step>`, `wf-ask-<step>`, the examples as chips that go to the input box) and what a blocked step waits on. `IntelligentView` routes the `workflow` kind and words the engine's fallback for internal mode.
+
+## Tests
+
+| Suite | What it checks | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| `packages/engine/src/researchPlanner.test.ts` | the whole workflow from one objective — every step's status, actions, sentence, questions and reason, the actions applied and the next step advanced, the planner writing nothing, the blocked steps naming what they wait on, the outputs done once produced, the deck after fieldwork, the summary and the description; the questionnaire's standard items linked to their constructs, the bespoke construct the model's, internal mode asking instead; the model tiers and the priced prompt; the score for a multi-item construct (and one under another name noticed), the recommended regression and crosstab (nothing twice), the KPIs with the score and the direction; the population, the noun, the questions that measure a name (by words and by the measure's own words), a framework keeping what was recorded; the workflow sentences | 4 tests (engine 1753 pass) |
+| `packages/ai/src/tiers.test.ts` | the small model when configured, else the large, else the default; `completeJson` sends the tier's model | 2 tests (ai 33 pass) |
